    "name": "central_D2_nonuniform_zero_flux_bc_ast_fixture",
    "description": "AST-expansion conformance fixture for grids/cartesian_nonuniform_1d/rules/central_D2_nonuniform_zero_flux_bc: a minimal consuming model binding N=8 at the import edge. The compound match D(D(u,x),x) must fire through the section-9.6.3 fixpoint (priority 10) and lower to the rule's makearray -- interior [2,7] holding the imported conservative finite-volume flux-difference stencil aggregate, faces i=1 and i=8 holding the zero-flux one-sided differences -- with all metaparameters folded, all apply_expression_template nodes inlined (including the two grid geometry templates the observeds xc and dxw apply to the node array xe), and the free-name geometry arrays xc and dxw surviving as index references. The model follows the grid's EDGE-ARRAY contract at N=8: it supplies the 9-node (x_nodes) quadratic-stretch array xe and derives xc = nonuniform_cell_center(xe), dxw = nonuniform_cell_width(xe), all spelled with the literal 8 because the edge binding closes N. The golden pins the byte-identical post-lowering AST -- including the grid-derived geometry observeds -- across bindings.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "conformance",
      "ast",
      "grid:cartesian_nonuniform_1d",
      "rule:central_D2_nonuniform_zero_flux_bc"
    ]
  },
